---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="Debrief's privacy model: local by default, no account, no telemetry, no bot. Transcription always runs on your computer; AI summaries do too unless you add your own cloud AI key.">
  <section style="padding: 56px 0 24px; max-width: 720px;">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Built so you never have to trust us.</h1>
    <p class="muted" style="font-size: 18px;">Debrief has no servers of its own, so there is nothing of yours on our side to leak, subpoena, train on, or breach.</p>
    <h2 style="margin-top: 40px;">What leaves your computer</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="line-height: 1.8;">
      <li><b>Model downloads</b> from Hugging Face and GitHub, when you ask for them, verified by SHA-256.</li>
      <li><b>An update check</b> against this project's GitHub releases (Settings > Updates; off means no request).</li>
      <li><b>Calendar links</b> you paste (.ics), fetched on your schedule, and a <b>webhook</b> you set up (off by default).</li>
      <li><b>Cloud AI, only if you turn it on</b> (off by default): transcript text, participant names, summaries and your questions go to the provider you pick (Anthropic Claude, OpenAI or OpenRouter) under your own key and their terms. Audio never leaves; transcription stays on-device.</li>
      <li><b>Your own model server</b> (Ollama, LM Studio), if you configure one. Then transcript text goes to that server, which is yours.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 style="margin-top: 40px;">What Debrief never does</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="line-height: 1.8;">
      <li>No account, sign-in, or license check.</li>
      <li>No telemetry, analytics, or crash reports.</li>
      <li>No bot in your meetings; other participants see nothing.</li>
      <li>No automatic recording, naming, or sharing. Every one of those needs a click.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 style="margin-top: 40px;">Share links</h2>
    <p class="muted">When you create a share link, Debrief serves that one recording from your computer to devices on the same network, only while Debrief is open and the link is enabled. Links are 128-bit random tokens. Disable or delete them from the meeting or from Settings.</p>
    <h2 style="margin-top: 40px;">Consent</h2>
    <p class="muted">Recording other people may require their consent where you live. Debrief makes it easy to record properly, and it is your responsibility to do so.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
